[
  {
    "sha": "89a85296ea0cb7c56ef50fd0e3b11a1614a615de",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDg5YTg1Mjk2ZWEwY2I3YzU2ZWY1MGZkMGUzYjExYTE2MTRhNjE1ZGU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T09:48:27Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T09:48:27Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(edm): wire no-core burnout - a pocket burnt out by offset rings, no core left\n\nA Wire Contour with a burnout clearance burns a closed pocket's whole\ninterior out: offset rings from the stated wall clearance inward, 0.9 x\nthe kerf offset apart, cut innermost first from one threading at the\nstart hole. A clearance below the kerf offset, a missing or misplaced\nstart hole, the punch side and a pattern that splits into islands are\nrefused by name; the no-core law (kerf swept out of the pocket, every\npiece left must be the wall's) refuses a core. #534's slug law reads a\nburnout as \"must free nothing\" (WireFinding::Core), and its kerf law\nblocks a ring that gouges a wall. The field rides the file mirror\n(burnout_clearance), and so the MCP params door; absent, every existing\ndocument, stamp and golden is unchanged.\n\nFixes #540\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
